Feature: API Tests for Donation

  @api @api_regression @api_donation @api_donation01
  Scenario: API_Create and Update Guest Donation (No Event, UPI Payment)
    Given I login with "cashier@nabarun.com" user using API
    Then I store "{RandomName} API" value as "DonorName" variable
    Then I store "{RandomEmail}" value as "DonorEmail" variable
    Then I store "9{RandomNumber:9}" value as "DonorPhone" variable
    Then I store "{RandomInt:100,999}" value as "DonationAmount" variable
    Then I send a POST request to "/donation/create/guest" with payload:
      """
      {
        "forEventId": null,
        "donorEmail": "{DonorEmail}",
        "donorName": "{DonorName}",
        "donorNumber": "{DonorPhone}",
        "amount": "{DonationAmount}"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 201
    Then I extract data from response using JSON token "responsePayload.id" and store it as "DonationId"
    Then I send a PATCH request to "/donation/{DonationId}/update" with payload:
      """
      {
        "status": "PAID",
        "paidOn": "{SystemDate}",
        "paidToAccountId": "ACC_TREASURER_PRINCIPAL",
        "paymentMethod": "UPI",
        "paidUsingUPI": "GPAY",
        "remarks": "Payment Done Updating using API"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    And I extract data from response using JSON token "responsePayload.transactionRef" and store it as "TransactionId"
    Then I send a POST request to "/dms/upload" with payload:
      """
      {
        "contentType": "image/jpeg",
        "fileBase64": "",
        "filename": "received_548688891947012.jpeg",
        "documentMapping": [
            {
                "entityId": "{DonationId}",
                "entityType": "DONATION"
            },
            {
                "entityId": "{TransactionId}",
                "entityType": "TRANSACTION"
            }
        ]
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 201
    Then I send a POST request to "/comments" with payload:
      """
      {
        "content": "Donation {DonationId} marked as paid with Transaction Ref {TransactionId} via API",
        "entityId": "{DonationId}",
        "entityType": "DONATION"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 201
    And I extract data from response using JSON token "responsePayload.id" and store it as "CommentId"
    Then I send a POST request to "/comments" with payload:
      """
      {
        "content": "Acknowledgement Provided by Cashier via API",
        "entityId": "{DonationId}",
        "entityType": "DONATION",
        "parentId": "{CommentId}"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 201
    Then I send a GET request to "/account/ACC_TREASURER_PRINCIPAL/transactions?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10&transactionRef={TransactionId}"
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    And The API response should have the following attributes
      | Attribute                                 | Value                   |
      | responsePayload.content[0].accTxnType     | Credit                  |
      | responsePayload.content[0].transactionRef | {TransactionId}         |
      | responsePayload.content[0].transferTo     | ACC_TREASURER_PRINCIPAL |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnAmount      | {DonationAmount}        |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnStatus      | SUCCESS                 |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnType        | IN                      |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnRefId       | {DonationId}            |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnRefType     | DONATION                |

  @api @api_regression @api_donation @api_donation02
  Scenario: API_Create and Update Guest Donation (With Event, Cash Payment, Status Transitions)
    Given I login with "cashier@nabarun.com" user using API
    Then I store "{RandomName} API" value as "DonorName" variable
    Then I store "{RandomEmail}" value as "DonorEmail" variable
    Then I store "9{RandomNumber:9}" value as "DonorPhone" variable
    Then I store "{RandomInt:100,999}" value as "DonationAmount" variable
    Then I store "{SystemDate [dd/MM/yyyy]}" value as "PaidOn" variable
    ## 1. Create Guest Donation (Linked to Project Event) - Status: RAISED
    Then I send a POST request to "/donation/create/guest" with payload:
      """
      {
        "forEventId": "EVT123",
        "donorEmail": "{DonorEmail}",
        "donorName": "{DonorName}",
        "donorNumber": "{DonorPhone}",
        "amount": "{DonationAmount}"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 201
    And I extract data from response using JSON token "responsePayload.id" and store it as "DonationId"
    And The API response should have the following attributes
      | Attribute                 | Value            |
      | responsePayload.status    | RAISED           |
      | responsePayload.amount    | {DonationAmount} |
      | responsePayload.donorName | {DonorName}      |
    ## 2. Update Status to 'Paid' (Cash Payment)
    Then I send a PATCH request to "/donation/{DonationId}/update" with payload:
      """
      {
        "status": "PAID",
        "paidOn": "{PaidOn}",
        "paidToAccountId": "ACC_TREASURER_PRINCIPAL",
        "paymentMethod": "CASH",
        "remarks": "Cash donation Test via API"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    And I extract data from response using JSON token "responsePayload.transactionRef" and store it as "TransactionRef"
    And The API response should have the following attributes
      | Attribute              | Value |
      | responsePayload.status | PAID  |
    ## 3. Verify Inward Transaction in Main Account
    Then I send a GET request to "/account/ACC_TREASURER_PRINCIPAL/transactions?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10&transactionRef={TransactionRef}"
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    And The API response should have the following attributes
      | Attribute                                 | Value            |
      | responsePayload.content[0].transactionRef | {TransactionRef} |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnType        | IN               |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnAmount      | {DonationAmount} |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnStatus      | SUCCESS          |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnRefId       | {DonationId}     |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnRefType     | DONATION         |
    ## 4. Perform 'Wrong Payment Update' (UPDATE_MISTAKE)
    Then I send a PATCH request to "/donation/{DonationId}/update" with payload:
      """
      {
        "status": "UPDATE_MISTAKE"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    And The API response should have the following attributes
      | Attribute              | Value          |
      | responsePayload.status | UPDATE_MISTAKE |
    ## 5. Verify Transaction Reversal (In/Out) in Accounts
    Then I send a GET request to "/account/ACC_TREASURER_PRINCIPAL/transactions?pageIndex=0&pageSize=10&transactionRef={TransactionRef}"
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    # Expected 2 transactions: Reversal (OUT) and Original (REVERSED)
    And The API response should have the following attributes
      | Attribute                                 | Value            |
      | responsePayload.content[0].transactionRef | {TransactionRef} |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnType        | OUT              |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnStatus      | SUCCESS          |
      | responsePayload.content[0].txnRefType     | TXN_REVERSE      |
      | responsePayload.content[1].transactionRef | {TransactionRef} |
      | responsePayload.content[1].txnType        | IN               |
      | responsePayload.content[1].txnStatus      | REVERSED         |
    ## 6. Transition Status back to 'Pending'
    Then I send a PATCH request to "/donation/{DonationId}/update" with payload:
      """
      {
        "status": "PENDING"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    And The API response should have the following attributes
      | Attribute              | Value   |
      | responsePayload.status | PENDING |
    ## 7. Final Status Transition to 'Cancelled'
    Then I send a PATCH request to "/donation/{DonationId}/update" with payload:
      """
      {
        "status": "CANCELLED",
        "reasonForCancel": "Test Cancellation via API"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    And The API response should have the following attributes
      | Attribute              | Value     |
      | responsePayload.status | CANCELLED |

