        "paidToAccountId": "ACC_TREASURER_PRINCIPAL",
        "paymentMethod": "NETBANKING",
        "remarks": "Net Banking test via API"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    And The API response should have the following attributes
      | Attribute              | Value |
      | responsePayload.status | PAID  |

  @api @api_regression @api_donation @api_donation04
  Scenario: API_Create and Update Member Regular Donation (Full Status Flow, UPI)
    Given I login with "cashier@nabarun.com" user using API
    ## 1. Authentication & Pre-Cleanup (Using existing cleanup step)
    Then I check and delete regular donation raised for "Member TestUser" this month
    ## 2. Search for Member to get donorId
    Then I send a GET request to "/users?firstName=Member&lastName=TestUser"
    Then The API response status code should be 200
    And I extract data from response using JSON token "responsePayload.content[0].id" and store it as "MemberId"
    ## 3. Initiate Member Regular Donation for Current Month
    Then I store "{RandomInt:100,999}" value as "DonationAmount" variable
    Then I store "{BeginningOfMonth [yyyy-MM-dd]}" value as "DonationStartDate" variable
    Then I store "{EndOfMonth [yyyy-MM-dd]}" value as "DonationEndDate" variable
    Then I send a POST request to "/donation/create" with payload:
      """
      {
        "type": "REGULAR",
        "donorId": "{MemberId}",
        "amount": "{DonationAmount}",
        "startDate": "{DonationStartDate}",
        "endDate": "{DonationEndDate}"
      }
      """
    Then The API response status code should be 201
    And I extract data from response using JSON token "responsePayload.id" and store it as "DonationId"
    ## 4. Transition through Various Statuses (Pending -> Payment Failed)
    # Transition to PENDING
    Then I send a PATCH request to "/donation/{DonationId}/update" with payload:
      """
      {
        "status": "PENDING"
      }
      """
